.TH NEXTPAD-PLUS-PLUS 1 "2026-05-13" "1.0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nextpad-plus-plus \- multi-tab text editor (Linux port of Notepad++)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nextpad-plus-plus
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nextpad-plus-plus
is a native Linux port of the Notepad++ text editor, built on Scintilla
and Lexilla with GTK 3. It supports multi-tab editing, syntax
highlighting for 50+ languages, user-defined languages, find/replace
with regex, macro recording, session save/restore, auto-backup, and a
plugin system compatible with the Notepad++ for macOS plugin SDK.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l \fIN\fR
Open the file at line \fIN\fR (1-based).
.TP
.B \-c \fIN\fR
Position the caret at column \fIN\fR (1-based; combine with \-l).
.TP
.B \-p \fIN\fR
Position the caret at byte offset \fIN\fR.
.TP
.B \-lang \fINAME\fR
Force a specific language (lexer) for the opened file.
.TP
.B \-udl \fINAME\fR
Force a user-defined language by name.
.TP
.B \-ro
Open the file read-only.
.TP
.B \-monitor
Tail-f mode \- auto-reload the file on every external change without prompting.
.SH "KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS"
File operations follow standard conventions (Ctrl+N, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S,
Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Q). See the View > Command Palette menu (Ctrl+Shift+P) for
the full action list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nextpad-plus-plus/
User configuration directory: session.xml, recentfiles.txt, backup/,
stylers.xml, userDefineLangs/, plugins/.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Notepad++ User Manual at https://npp-user-manual.org/.
